# Git Publish Gate

Agents MUST NOT publish to GitHub on their own. When they do push (user-requested), local CI is mandatory every time.

## Required

- **Do not** run `git push`, `git push --force`, or any remote publish unless the user **explicitly** asks to push/publish in that message.
- Completing work or syncing artifacts does **not** imply push permission.
- Local `git commit` also requires an **explicit** user request to commit.

## When the user asks to push

1. Load skill **`edunudg-pre-push-ci`** (required — not optional)
2. Commit first **only if** the user also asked to commit
3. Run **`pnpm ci:local`** as a **separate** shell command (full GitHub CI mirror) until exit 0 — auto-fix failures; do not ask permission to fix
4. Only then `git push` (only the refs the user asked for)

### Enforcement layers (all active)

| Layer | Behavior |
|-------|----------|
| This rule + `edunudg-pre-push-ci` | Agent must run CI before attempting push |
| `.cursor/hooks/gate-git-push.sh` | **Denies** `git push` without a recent green `.git/edunudg-ci-local.ok` stamp for HEAD |
| `.githooks/pre-push` | Runs `pnpm ci:local` (or accepts recent stamp) before allowing the push |

Bypass only with user-approved `SKIP_CI_LOCAL=1` (Cursor hook asks for confirmation).

Skipping RLS/e2e requires the user to allow that skip in the same message.

## After local work (no push ask)

Leave changes uncommitted/unpushed. Tell the user what is ready and wait for “commit”, “push”, or “commit and push”.

## Forbidden

- Pushing without a green `pnpm ci:local` for the **current HEAD**
- Chaining `git commit && git push` without `pnpm ci:local` in between
- Pushing to “unblock CI” while local CI is red or unrun
- Treating a prior push or prior CI run as standing permission for the next one
- Asking whether to run local CI before push — just run it
- Inventing `SKIP_CI_LOCAL=1` without explicit user emergency approval
